+# CLI Time Tracker — Contract
+
+## Public API
+
+All exports from `src/index.ts`:
+
+### `createTracker(options?: CreateTrackerOptions): TimeTracker`
+Factory function that creates a time tracker instance.
+
+```typescript
+interface CreateTrackerOptions {
+  dbPath?: string; // Default: './time-tracker.json'
+}
+```
+
+### `TimeTracker` interface methods
+
+| Method | Signature | Description |
+|--------|-----------|-------------|
+| `start` | `(name: string) => TimeEntry` | Start a named timer. Auto-stops any running timer first. Throws if name is empty. |
+| `stop` | `() => TimeEntry` | Stop the running timer. Throws if nothing is running. Returns the stopped entry. |
+| `getLog` | `(opts?: { since?: Date }) => TimeEntry[]` | Return all entries, optionally filtered by start date >= `since`. Running entries started before `since` are still included. |
+| `getSummary` | `() => Record<string, number>` | Return total ms per task name. Running tasks use current time. |
+| `getActiveTask` | `() => string \| null` | Return current running task name, or null. |
+
+### `TimeEntry` interface
+
+```typescript
+interface TimeEntry {
+  name: string;
+  start: Date;
+  stop?: Date; // undefined if still running
+}
+```
+
+## Behaviors & Verification
+
+### Core Operations
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 1 | `start("name")` creates an active entry with a start time and no stop time | entry has `name`, `start` instanceof Date, `stop` is undefined |
+| 2 | `stop()` sets `stop` time on the active entry | after stop, entry.stop is a Date |
+| 3 | Starting a new task auto-stops the previous one | start "a" → start "b" → entries have "a".stop set, "b".stop undefined |
+| 4 | `stop()` when nothing is running throws an Error | call stop twice, second call throws |
+
+### Query Operations
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 5 | `getLog()` returns all entries | after 3 start/stop cycles, getLog has 3 entries |
+| 6 | `getLog({ since })` filters entries starting after that date | start "a" (t=1), start "b" (t=3) → getLog({since: t=2}) only has "b" |
+| 7 | `getLog({ since })` includes running entries started before the since date | start "a" (t=1), getLog({since: t=2}) includes "a" because it's still running |
+| 8 | `getSummary()` returns object keyed by task name with total ms | start "a" (t=0) → stop (t=100) → getSummary returns `{ a: 100000 }` (100 real ms) |
+| 9 | `getSummary()` combines multiple entries for same name | start "a" (t=0) → stop (t=100) → start "a" (t=200) → stop (t=300) → summary has `{ a: 200000 }` |
+| 10 | `getActiveTask()` returns current task name or null | start "a" → getActiveTask() returns "a"; stop → getActiveTask() returns null |
+
+### Persistence
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 11 | Data persists across instances | create tracker1, start "a", stop; create tracker2 with same path, getLog includes "a" |
+| 12 | Creates data file + parent dirs if missing | Use path in non-existent dir; file is created automatically |
+| 13 | File path is configurable | Pass `dbPath` option; data saved/loaded from that path |
+
+### Edge Cases
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 14 | `start("")` throws an error | Call start with empty/whitespace-only string → throws Error |
+| 15 | Unicode/emoji task names work | start "🏃‍♂️测试" → entry.name matches; getSummary key matches |
+| 16 | `getLog({ since })` with future date returns empty array | start "a", getLog({since: farFuture}) → [] |
+| 17 | `getLog({ since })` with old date returns all entries | start "a", getLog({since: ancient past}) → includes "a" |
+| 18 | `getSummary()` with no entries returns `{}` | Fresh tracker with no activity → {} |
+| 19 | `getLog()` with no entries returns `[]` | Fresh tracker with no activity → [] |
+| 20 | Rapid sequential start calls do not corrupt data | start "a" → start "b" → start "c" → all 3 entries present, "a".stop and "b".stop are Dates, "c".stop is undefined |
+
+### Data Integrity
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 21 | Multiple start/stop cycles accumulate correctly | 10 start/stop cycles → getLog has 10 entries |
+| 22 | Log entries have correct shape | Every entry has `name` (string), `start` (Date), and either `stop` (Date) or `stop` undefined |
+| 23 | Summary durations are positive numbers | All values in getSummary result are > 0 |
+| 24 | `stop()` returns the stopped entry | stop() return value matches the entry that was stopped |
+| 25 | Auto-stop returns new entry; previous task is stopped | `start("a")` returns entry a; `start("b")` returns entry b; entry a has stop set |
+
+## Non-Goals
+- No CLI interface (this is a library)
+- No concurrent timer support (only one active timer at a time)
+- No runtime dependencies beyond Node.js built-ins
